<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sivasagar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sibsagar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sivasagar, formerly Sibsagar, is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-assam">Upper Assam</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and the headquarters of Sivasagar district. It grew around the great tank dug in the 1730s under Ahom royal patronage, and lies close to the former Ahom capitals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garhgaon">Garhgaon</a> and Rangpur. Its monuments, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivadol">Sivadol</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rang-ghar">Rang Ghar</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talatal-ghar">Talatal Ghar</a>, make it the main centre of Ahom heritage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sivasagar.jpg" alt="Sivasagar" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shyam Kaanu · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sivasagar_Night_View.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
